# nginx FHS migration: runtime state /run/nginx -> /var/run/nginx.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - PID file: a new master refuses to start while an old master holds
#   the listen sockets (bind fails: no silent takeover). A dead
#   master's pidfile is overwritten on start. Nothing is deleted.
# - Lock file (accept mutex): flock semantics, stale-safe by design.
# - New /var/run/nginx: created with nginx:nginx 0755 by checkpath
#   (OpenRC) and tmpfiles.d (systemd); converged here on upgrade.
# - Old /run/nginx: volatile residue. Removed once empty (old daemon
#   gone); left in place and reported while the old daemon still
#   runs. /run itself is tmpfs and vanishes on reboot regardless.

dir /var/run/nginx 0755 nginx nginx
rmdir-if-empty /run/nginx
